<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/heuristics-and-biases-program> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The research program, launched by Amos Tversky and Daniel Kahneman around 1970, that explains intuitive judgment under uncertainty as the use of a few general-purpose heuristics (such as representativeness, availability and anchoring) which are usually serviceable but produce predictable, systematic errors when compared with normative rules." .
