<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/illicit-major> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The syllogistic fallacy committed when the major term (the predicate of the conclusion) is distributed in the conclusion but undistributed in the major premise, so the conclusion says something about the whole of a class that the premises described only in part." .
