<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/pragma-dialectics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A theory of argumentation, developed by Frans van Eemeren and Rob Grootendorst at the University of Amsterdam, that models argument as an exchange of speech acts aimed at resolving a difference of opinion on the merits, and defines a fallacy as any move that breaks one of the rules of an ideal critical discussion." .
