<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/prior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Aristotle's two-book treatise (c. 350 BCE) that founded formal logic: it classifies two-premise deductions into three figures, proves the imperfect ones by reducing them to a handful of self-evident first-figure moods, shows invalidity by counterexample, and extends the system to necessity and possibility." .
